From 24128ab742af1f8d85088d191d92ff7ccaefbd3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yangsonglin13 <yangsonglin566@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:56:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] perf(rfork): deduplicate tensor scans and stabilize
 readable IDs

Use layered BFS and deterministic canonical tensor paths to avoid repeated
shared-object scans. Preserve registered parameter and buffer names over
shorter aliases, encode typed container keys, and reject ambiguous labels.

Reuse registration inventories, captured NPU formats and final-layout digests.
Refresh the live-model digest before deferred seed publication. Cover aliases,
key collisions, scan reuse, digest lifecycle and registration cleanup, and
update the bilingual guide.

Includes cherry-picked commit 20a3915f3f3d162a67bdd98597c1202dc6a99a2f.

Co-authored-by: AbyssSkb <abyssskb@outlook.com>
Signed-off-by: AbyssSkb <abyssskb@outlook.com>
Signed-off-by: yangsonglin13 <yangsonglin566@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 97df28e9454acedd193f7bc729b9be7d5566f44d)
Signed-off-by: AbyssSkb <abyssskb@outlook.com>
